item.text:
Exposure summary: Biden had material authority over U.S. nuclear declaratory policy, alliance signaling, crisis messaging, and the budget request, but the practical posture was constrained by Congress, the Pentagon review process, allies, and Russia’s escalation in Ukraine. I did not score.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E1","title":"Department of Defense Releases its 2022 Strategic Reviews – National Defense Strategy, Nuclear Posture Review, and Missile Defense Review","publisher":"U.S. Department of Defense","publication_date":"2022-10-27","url":"https://www.defense.gov/News/Releases/Release/Article/3201683/department-of-defense-releases-its-2022-strategic-reviews-national-defense-stra/?idU=1","claim":"The 2022 NPR says the fundamental role of U.S. nuclear weapons is deterrence and that use would be considered only in extreme circumstances.","locator":"line 218","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous official policy release from the responsible department.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden as commander-in-chief through the administration's nuclear posture.","contrary_evidence":["The same posture preserves a deterrent and does not adopt sole purpose or no-first-use."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.4","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E2","title":"DOD Releases National Defense Strategy, Missile Defense, Nuclear Posture Reviews","publisher":"U.S. Department of Defense","publication_date":"2022-10-27","url":"https://www.defense.gov/News/News-Stories/Article/article/3202438/dod-releases-national-defense-strategy-missile-defense-nuclear-posture-reviews/","claim":"The department released the NDS, NPR, and MDR together and said the integrated process was meant to match resources to goals.","locator":"article lede","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official contemporaneous explanation of the administration's strategic-review process.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Biden's administration set the review process and the strategic framing.","contrary_evidence":["Integration does not itself prove risk reduction or implementation success."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E3","title":"Official Says Nuclear Posture Review Gives Options","publisher":"U.S. Department of Defense","publication_date":"2022-11-01","url":"https://www.defense.gov/News/News-Stories/Article/Article/3206842/official-says-nuclear-posture-review-gives-options/","claim":"The Pentagon described the NPR as giving the United States a range of options for nuclear threats against the homeland, allies, and partners.","locator":"article lede","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official explanatory follow-up to the NPR release, but still an interpretive defense-side framing.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Within the 2022 release window.","ruler_attribution":"Reflects Biden administration policy as implemented by DoD officials.","contrary_evidence":["The article is descriptive of options, not a proof of safer outcomes."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E4","title":"The 2022 Nuclear Posture Review: Arms Control Subdued By Military Rivalry","publisher":"Federation of American Scientists","publication_date":"2022-10-27","url":"https://fas.org/publication/2022-nuclear-posture-review/","claim":"FAS says the 2022 NPR rejected sole-purpose and no-first-use approaches for now and preserved a broad deterrence posture.","locator":"lines 50-52 and 82-84","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialized independent nuclear-policy analysis with direct discussion of the NPR text.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly on the 2022 NPR release.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to Biden's own posture review, though filtered through analyst interpretation.","contrary_evidence":["The same analysis notes the NPR still gestures toward reducing nuclear reliance where possible."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.4","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E5","title":"The Biden Nuclear Posture Review: Obstacles to Reducing Reliance on Nuclear Weapons","publisher":"Arms Control Association","publication_date":"2022-01","url":"https://www.armscontrol.org/act/2022-01/features/biden-nuclear-posture-review-obstacles-reducing-reliance-nuclear-weapons","claim":"ACA says Biden entered office aiming to reduce nuclear reliance and adopt sole-purpose language, but the NPR process faced strong institutional resistance and was unlikely to achieve that goal cleanly.","locator":"lines 79-83","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Expert arms-control analysis written before the NPR was finalized, useful for intended direction and constraints.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Inherited baseline and early 2022 policy process.","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Biden's intended nuclear policy and the institutional barriers around it.","contrary_evidence":["This is a pre-release forecast, not an outcome audit."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.7","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E6","title":"Biden's Disappointing Nuclear Posture Review","publisher":"Arms Control Association","publication_date":"2022-12","url":"https://www.armscontrol.org/act/2022-12/focus/bidens-disappointing-nuclear-posture-review","claim":"ACA argues the 2022 NPR maintained dangerous reliance on nuclear threats, sent muddled messages, and preserved a large modernization program.","locator":"lines 79-85 and 95","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent, detailed critique written after the NPR release with direct engagement on policy content.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Biden's final 2022 posture text and his remaining opportunity to adjust it.","contrary_evidence":["The analysis also notes the administration still pursued effective arms-control negotiations."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.4","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E7","title":"NNSA's annual Stockpile Stewardship and Management Plan delivered to Congress","publisher":"Department of Energy, National Nuclear Security Administration","publication_date":"2022-03-16","url":"https://www.energy.gov/nnsa/articles/nnsas-annual-stockpile-stewardship-and-management-plan-delivered-congress","claim":"NNSA's FY2022 plan says the United States is maintaining a safe, secure, effective stockpile without underground nuclear explosive testing.","locator":"line 173","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary official budget-and-safety document from the nuclear security enterprise.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly relevant to 2022 posture and command-and-control safety baseline.","ruler_attribution":"Reflects Biden-era nuclear stewardship through NNSA and DoD requirements.","contrary_evidence":["This is stewardship of an inherited arsenal, not evidence of disarmament or major risk reduction by itself."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E8","title":"U.S. removes over 30 kilograms of highly enriched uranium from Japan","publisher":"Department of Energy, National Nuclear Security Administration","publication_date":"2022-05-23","url":"https://www.energy.gov/nnsa/articles/us-removes-over-30-kilograms-highly-enriched-uranium-japan","claim":"Biden and Kishida announced the removal of more than 30 kilograms of HEU from three Japanese sites, reducing weapons-usable material and nuclear-device risk.","locator":"lines 174-184","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary official nonproliferation action with clear factual details and direct presidential attribution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden's diplomatic and nonproliferation agenda with Japan.","contrary_evidence":["This is a discrete nonproliferation success, not a broad arms-control settlement."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.6","1B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E9","title":"FY 2022 Presidential Budget for NNSA released","publisher":"Department of Energy, National Nuclear Security Administration","publication_date":"2021-05-28","url":"https://www.energy.gov/nnsa/articles/fy-2022-presidential-budget-nnsa-released","claim":"The Biden administration's FY2022 NNSA budget request funded the tools needed to keep the stockpile safe, secure, effective, and to reduce proliferation and terrorism risk.","locator":"opening paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget request from the administration's nuclear-security enterprise.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Inherited baseline shaping the 2022 nuclear-security enterprise.","ruler_attribution":"Biden administration budget authority, though the line reflects implementation through DOE/NNSA rather than personal action.","contrary_evidence":["A funded enterprise still preserves modernization and deterrence rather than disarmament."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E10","title":"Readout of President Biden's Meeting with President Andrzej Duda of Poland","publisher":"The American Presidency Project","publication_date":"2022-03-26","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/readout-president-bidens-meeting-with-president-andrzej-duda-poland","claim":"Biden reaffirmed the United States' unwavering commitment to Article 5 and support for NATO allies while discussing Ukraine and European security.","locator":"lines 62-63","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reliable transcript-style reproduction of an official presidential readout.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 Ukraine crisis and NATO reassurance period.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden as the public face of alliance signaling and crisis management.","contrary_evidence":["Alliance reassurance is not the same as nuclear-risk reduction."],"lenses":["1B.5","1B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E11","title":"Remarks With President Andrzej Duda of Poland in a Briefing on Humanitarian Efforts for Ukraine in Jasionka, Poland","publisher":"The American Presidency Project","publication_date":"2022-03-25","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-with-president-andrzej-duda-poland-briefing-humanitarian-efforts-for-ukraine","claim":"Biden said the key task was keeping democracies united to curb the devastation caused by Putin's war.","locator":"line 64","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Transcript-style reproduction of Biden's public remarks, useful for contemporaneous crisis signaling.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 invasion response window.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden's crisis diplomacy and alliance coordination.","contrary_evidence":["This is humanitarian and coalition messaging, not an explicit nuclear de-escalation directive."],"lenses":["1B.8","1B.5"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E12","title":"Reading the Nuclear Tea Leaves: Policy and Posture in the Biden Administration","publisher":"CSIS","publication_date":"2021","url":"https://www.csis.org/analysis/reading-nuclear-tea-leaves-policy-and-posture-biden-administration","claim":"CSIS notes that Biden moved quickly to extend New START and that allies generally saw the early posture as more reassuring than the Trump-era approach, even while modernization remained intact.","locator":"New START and concluding posture discussion","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialized nuclear-policy analysis with direct discussion of Biden-era posture and allied reaction.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Inherited baseline and early Biden posture shaping the 2022 environment.","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Biden's nuclear-policy choices and allied-management constraints.","contrary_evidence":["The same analysis says the review preserved strong deterrence and modernization choices."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.7","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E13","title":"Deterring Nuclear Weapons Use in Ukraine","publisher":"CSIS","publication_date":"2022-10-14","url":"https://www.csis.org/analysis/deterring-nuclear-weapons-use-ukraine","claim":"CSIS says the Biden administration had to balance avoiding overt public nuclear threats with using private deterrence signals to keep Putin from escalating.","locator":"line 249","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Focused analytical piece on the exact crisis dynamic Biden faced in 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 Ukraine nuclear-risk crisis.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden's crisis-management choices toward Russia.","contrary_evidence":["This describes a balancing act, not a clearly proven reduction in nuclear risk."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E14","title":"Biden suggests Putin's threats mean a prospect of Armageddon","publisher":"The Washington Post","publication_date":"2022-10-06","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/10/06/biden-putin-nuclear-armageddon/","claim":"The article reports that Biden publicly warned Putin's nuclear threats could lead to Armageddon and that he was looking for Putin's off-ramp.","locator":"lines 24-27","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous major-outlet reporting on Biden's unscripted rhetoric and its immediate interpretation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 nuclear-escalation scare over Ukraine.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden's own rhetoric, though reported by a secondary source.","contrary_evidence":["The remark was rhetorical and not itself a policy change."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E15","title":"How likely is the use of nuclear weapons by Russia?","publisher":"Chatham House","publication_date":"2022-09-23","url":"https://www.chathamhouse.org/2022/03/how-likely-use-nuclear-weapons-russia","claim":"Chatham House describes the Russian invasion as creating serious nuclear risks and highlights the danger that escalation and miscalculation could lead to nuclear use.","locator":"section on Russian nuclear threats and escalation risk","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"High-quality independent analysis of the crisis environment, but not a direct source on Biden's decisions.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly relevant background to the 2022 crisis Biden was managing.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect, as crisis context that constrained Biden's choices.","contrary_evidence":["The piece is about Russian behavior, not an evaluation of Biden's own conduct."],"lenses":["1B.8","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E16","title":"Russia's Catch-all Nuclear Rhetoric in Its War against Ukraine","publisher":"Stiftung Wissenschaft und Politik","publication_date":"2022-10-19","url":"https://www.swp-berlin.org/en/publication/russias-catch-all-nuclear-rhetoric-in-its-war-against-ukraine","claim":"SWP characterizes Russian nuclear signaling in Ukraine as a mix of deterrence, dissuasion, and compellence, which clarifies the escalation environment Biden faced.","locator":"title and introductory summary","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Specialist foreign-policy research institute with direct crisis analysis, useful mainly as context.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly relevant to the 2022 escalation environment.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context for Biden's crisis choices, not a direct attribution claim.","contrary_evidence":["This is a Russia-focused analysis rather than a Biden performance assessment."],"lenses":["1B.8","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"evidence_id":"E17","title":"Biden denounces Russia at U.N., says Putin 'shamelessly violated' charter","publisher":"CBS News","publication_date":"2022-09-21","url":"https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/biden-united-nations-speech-general-assembly-russia-putin-ukraine/","claim":"CBS reported that Biden used the UN General Assembly to denounce Russia's invasion and Putin's overt nuclear threats as a charter violation.","locator":"headline and article summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Reputable contemporaneous media report on a major public speech, but still secondary reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Biden's public crisis messaging.","contrary_evidence":["The report captures rhetoric and framing, not a documented operational de-escalation step."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.8"]}

Search ledger: candidates found approximately 58, documents opened 30, duplicate or syndicated mirrors collapsed 14, irrelevant or out-of-period items 9, inaccessible or technical-error pages 7, accepted distinct URLs 17.

Material gaps and next-best directions:
- Direct openable archived White House, State, and UN/IAEA pages for Biden's NPT speech and U.S. nuclear-policy statements were partly inaccessible in this pass; next step should use the PDF originals or alternate archives for `NPT/CONF.2020/57`, the U.S. NPT side-event remarks, and any IAEA press conference pages.
- 1B.3 and 1B.7 still need stronger direct evidence on named expert appointments, oversight structures, and command-and-control safety decisions; next query family should target State/DOE appointment notices, NSC staffing, and advisory-board records.
- 1B.6 and 1B.9 are still thin on dual-use and proliferation restraint beyond the Japan HEU removal and AUKUS-related context; next best source family is `iaea.org`, `ctbto.org`, `nti.org`, and careful Reuters follow-up on AUKUS safeguards.
- The crisis-response picture is best on 1B.8, but still mostly rhetorical and alliance-facing; a later pass should look for declassified or contemporaneous records on backchannel communication, deconfliction, and nuclear-risk signaling with Russia.
